@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+## Why
+
+The desk needs to see at a glance what can still be rented for a given period, instead of trying `book` item by item.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `availability({ start, end, kind? })` to the rental service. It returns the sorted ids of the equipment of that kind (any kind when `kind` is omitted) that is free for the whole period.
+- Rentals: the "no cancel operation" requirement lists the exposed operations; it now includes `availability`.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- `rental`: adds an availability requirement and updates the exposed-operations scenario.
+
+## Scope
+
+- In scope: the read-only availability query for rentals, using the same whole-day UTC periods and overlap rule as `book`.
+- Out of scope: cancellations, season (April to October) enforcement, prices in the result, lessons and customers.
+
+No runtime dependency is introduced.
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/index.ts` (service interface and implementation), `test/rental.test.ts`. No dependency or package changes.
